{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07dba-037c-7562-bb6d-27534398ea11"},"sequence":265,"recorded_at":1780531400000525,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a742de3f-70ab-4a15-a8ac-23d4abf2b871"},"task_id":"a742de3f-70ab-4a15-a8ac-23d4abf2b871","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"a742de3f-70ab-4a15-a8ac-23d4abf2b871","span_id":"20a41f706da1737b"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07dba-037c-7562-bb6d-27534398ea11"},"sequence":266,"recorded_at":1780531400000527,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a742de3f-70ab-4a15-a8ac-23d4abf2b871"},"task_id":"a742de3f-70ab-4a15-a8ac-23d4abf2b871","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a742de3f-70ab-4a15-a8ac-23d4abf2b871","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-35dbcs/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(4589 line(s) above)\n4590|- <code>subject_id</code>, the logical session or workspace scope;\n4591|- <code>created_by_host_id</code>;\n4592|- diagnostic <code>created_at</code>; and\n4593|- optional namespaced <code>extensions</code>.\n4594|\n4595|The storage path MUST be derived from the digest, never from an untrusted\n4596|display name. A digest collision or same-ID/different-bytes observation is an\n4597|integrity emergency: both inputs MUST be quarantined and sync MUST stop for the\n4598|affected peer.\n4599|\n4600|### 10.2 Content-addressed blobs\n4601|\n4602|A blob is an uninterpreted byte sequence identified by SHA-256. Blob metadata\n4603|MUST live in a manifest, not in the blob path. Before publishing a record that\n4604|references a blob, the writer MUST fsync the blob, verify its size and digest,\n4605|and atomically install it in the object store.\n4606|\n4607|Provider/task-board blobs can contain sensitive project history. Logs and\n4608|metrics MUST record digest, size, and media type only, never blob contents.\n4609|\n4610|Every transferred blob has a Blob Descriptor with schema\n4611|<code>urn:ax:schema:blob</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Chunks MUST be\n4612|sorted, contiguous, non-overlapping, start at offset zero, and cover exactly\n4613|<code>size</code> bytes:\n4614|\n4615|The descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4616|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n4617|<code>descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>,\n4618|<code>size:uint53</code>, <code>media_type:string[1..255]</code>, and\n4619|<code>chunks:BlobChunk[0..32768]</code>. <code>media_type</code> is a lowercase\n4620|ASCII <code>type/subtype</code> without parameters. BlobChunk is closed and\n4621|contains exactly <code>index:uint32</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>,\n4622|<code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and <code>chunk_id:digest</code>. Indexes\n4623|start at zero and increase by one. An empty blob has size zero and no chunks;\n4624|a non-empty blob has at least one.\n4625|\n4626|~~~json\n4627|{\n4628|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:blob\",\n4629|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4630|  \"descriptor_id\": \"sha256:390c8f21900483a010c1cbc3f9be01afebcf6e4da87263ba09fc5776dd6503ee\",\n4631|  \"blob_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\",\n4632|  \"size\": 11,\n4633|  \"media_type\": \"application/octet-stream\",\n4634|  \"chunks\": [\n4635|    {\n4636|      \"index\": 0,\n4637|      \"offset\": 0,\n4638|      \"size\": 11,\n4639|      \"chunk_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\"\n4640|    }\n4641|  ]\n4642|}\n4643|~~~\n4644|\n4645|The descriptor ID is its canonical object digest with\n4646|<code>descriptor_id</code> omitted. The example describes the eleven raw bytes\n4647|<code>ax-example\\n</code>, whose unpadded base64url form is\n4648|<code>YXgtZXhhbXBsZQo</code>; the one last-chunk digest therefore equals the\n4649|whole-blob digest. Empty blobs have an empty chunk array. Protocol 1.0.0 permits\n4650|at most 32,768 chunks in one Blob Descriptor, so one blob is at most 128 GiB.\n4651|A larger file MUST fail capture with <code>capability_unavailable</code> before\n4652|publishing a partial manifest.\n4653|\n4654|### 10.3 Transfer Chunk Descriptor\n4655|\n4656|The transfer unit is a fixed 4 MiB chunk except the last chunk. Chunk schema is\n4657|<code>urn:ax:schema:chunk</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n4658|\n4659|The Transfer Chunk Descriptor is closed and contains exactly\n4660|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n4661|<code>blob_id:digest</code>, <code>index:uint32</code>,\n4662|<code>offset:uint53</code>, <code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and\n4663|<code>chunk_id:digest</code>. It has no extension map. Offset MUST equal index\n4664|times 4,194,304; every non-final chunk has that exact size.\n4665|\n4666|~~~json\n4667|{\n4668|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:chunk\",\n4669|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4670|  \"blob_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\",\n4671|  \"index\": 0,\n4672|  \"offset\": 0,\n4673|  \"size\": 11,\n4674|  \"chunk_id\": \"sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50\"\n4675|}\n4676|~~~\n4677|\n4678|Chunk digests are over raw chunk bytes. A receiver MUST validate every chunk\n4679|before marking it present and MUST validate the complete blob after assembly.\n4680|Chunk identity is transfer metadata; the whole blob digest is storage identity.\n4681|\n4682|### 10.4 Transfer Manifest\n4683|\n4684|Transfer Manifest schema <code>urn:ax:schema:transfer-manifest</code> version\n4685|<code>1.0.0</code> describes one immutable snapshot. Its top-level object is\n4686|closed and contains exactly:\n4687|\n4688|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n4689|| --- | --- | --- |\n4690|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Transfer Manifest schema identifier |\n4691|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n4692|| <code>manifest_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n4693|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>workspace_group</code>, <code>workspace_tree</code>, <code>provider</code>, <code>task_board</code>, or <code>composite</code> |\n4694|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Group, workspace, or session selected by kind |\n4695|| <code>base_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for an initial capture with no predecessor checkpoint |\n4696|| <code>entries</code> | ManifestEntry[0..65536] | Sorted bytewise by normalized path |\n4697|| <code>child_manifest_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..1024] | Path-disjoint child/partition closure |\n4698|| <code>workspace_snapshot</code> | WorkspaceSnapshot or null | Non-null only for <code>workspace_group</code> |\n4699|| <code>provider_identity_record_id</code> | digest or null | Non-null only for <code>provider</code> |\n4700|| <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> | digest or null | Non-null only for <code>task_board</code> |\n4701|| <code>excluded_classes</code> | sorted unique string[0..128] | Applied exclusion-policy classes |\n4702|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Capturing host |\n4703|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n4704|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n4705|\n4706|The kind invariants are exact:\n4707|\n4708|- <code>workspace_group</code> uses the Workspace Group ID as subject, requires\n4709|  a non-null workspace snapshot and at least one child, and requires empty\n4710|  entries plus null provider/task-board IDs;\n4711|- <code>workspace_tree</code> uses one Workspace ID as subject, requires null\n4712|  snapshot/provider/task-board fields, and contains entries and optional\n4713|  path-partition children;\n4714|- <code>provider</code> uses a Session ID, requires a provider identity record,\n4715|  and requires null snapshot/task-board fields;\n4716|- <code>task_board</code> uses a Session ID, requires a bundle ID, and requires\n4717|  null snapshot/provider fields; and\n4718|- <code>composite</code> requires at least one child, empty entries, and all\n4719|  three tagged fields null.\n4720|\n4721|TerminalBackend runtime state is never a Transfer Manifest kind, child, or\n4722|entry. Capture selection MUST exclude Terminal Instance Bindings and backend-\n4723|local durable metadata; native references and generations; runtime IPC; Unix/\n4724|tmux sockets; named pipes; attach endpoints/tokens; relay credentials; backend\n4725|auth state/private live databases; GUI/login attestations; provider credentials;\n4726|PIDs/handles; terminal state/output/scrollback; and live-process observations.\n4727|Applicable exclusions MUST be named in <code>excluded_classes</code>; omission\n4728|from that diagnostic array never permits the bytes to enter a manifest. Only\n4729|the sanitized immutable evidence admitted to the Mesh RPC 4\n4730|<code>terminal_backend_evidence</code> namespace is replicable, and it travels\n4731|as schema objects through RPC inventory rather than as Transfer Manifest file\n4732|entries.\n4733|\n4734|Every direct-session checkpoint references one <code>provider</code> manifest,\n4735|even for a backend-only identity with zero entries. Every task-board checkpoint\n4736|references the bundle directly and MAY additionally transfer a\n4737|<code>task_board</code> manifest. A composite MUST NOT duplicate a child's\n4738|entries.\n4739|\n4740|<code>ManifestEntry</code> is a closed tagged union. Fields not listed for a\n4741|variant are forbidden:\n4742|\n4743|| Tag | Exact members |\n4744|| --- | --- |\n4745|| <code>type = directory</code> | <code>path:path</code>, <code>type:directory</code>, <code>mode:uint32[0..4095]</code> |\n4746|| <code>type = file</code> | <code>path:path</code>, <code>type:file</code>, <code>mode:uint32[0..4095]</code>, <code>size:uint53</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>, <code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code> |\n4747|| <code>type = symlink</code> | <code>path:path</code>, <code>type:symlink</code>, <code>mode:uint32[0..4095]</code>, <code>target:string[1..4096]</code> |\n4748|| <code>type = hardlink</code> | <code>path:path</code>, <code>type:hardlink</code>, <code>mode:uint32[0..4095]</code>, <code>target_path:path</code> |\n4749|\n4750|Directory, symlink, and hardlink positive fragments are:\n4751|\n4752|~~~json\n4753|{\"path\":\"src\",\"type\":\"directory\",\"mode\":493}\n4754|~~~\n4755|\n4756|~~~json\n4757|{\"path\":\"current\",\"type\":\"symlink\",\"mode\":511,\"target\":\"releases/v1\"}\n4758|~~~\n4759|\n4760|~~~json\n4761|{\"path\":\"README-copy.md\",\"type\":\"hardlink\",\"mode\":420,\"target_path\":\"README.md\"}\n4762|~~~\n4763|\n4764|Every file entry MUST reference a Blob Descriptor whose blob ID and size equal\n4765|the entry. A hardlink target MUST name an earlier file entry with the same mode.\n4766|A symlink target is interpreted relative to its containing directory and MUST\n4767|resolve within the materialization root after lexical and filesystem checks.\n4768|Absolute or escaping targets fail. Entries and child partitions MUST contain\n4769|no duplicate, overlapping, or destination-case-colliding path.\n4770|\n4771|<code>WorkspaceSnapshot</code> is a closed object containing exactly\n4772|<code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code> and\n4773|<code>members:WorkspaceSnapshotMember[1..256]</code>. Its group ID equals the\n4774|manifest subject, and its members correspond one-for-one, in workspace-ID\n4775|order, with the Workspace Group Record. A snapshot member is one of these\n4776|closed variants; neither variant has an extension point:\n4777|\n4778|| Tag | Exact members |\n4779|| --- | --- |\n4780|| <code>kind = git</code> | <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:git</code>, <code>group_relative_path:path</code>, <code>repository_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>remotes:GitRemote[1..16]</code>, <code>head:GitHead</code>, <code>upstream_ref:git-ref&#124;null</code>, <code>object_pack:GitObjectPack</code>, <code>index:GitIndex</code>, <code>working_tree_manifest_id:digest</code>, <code>submodules:GitSubmodule[0..256]</code>, <code>features:GitFeatures</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]</code>, <code>materialization_policy:shared_checkout&#124;separate_worktree</code> |\n4781|| <code>kind = managed_tree</code> | <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:managed_tree</code>, <code>group_relative_path:path</code>, <code>tree_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>tree_manifest_id:digest</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]</code>, <code>materialization_policy:shared_tree&#124;separate_copy</code> |\n4782|\n4783|The Git embedded types are closed and exact:\n4784|\n4785|| Type | Exact members and constraints |\n4786|| --- | --- |\n4787|| <code>GitRemote</code> | <code>name:string[1..128]</code>, <code>fetch_url:sanitized-git-URL</code>, <code>push_url:sanitized-git-URL&#124;null</code>; sorted by name, no duplicate |\n4788|| <code>GitHead</code> | <code>mode:branch&#124;detached&#124;unborn</code>, <code>oid:git-oid&#124;null</code>, <code>ref:git-ref&#124;null</code>; branch has both, detached has only oid, unborn has only a <code>refs/heads/</code> ref |\n4789|| <code>GitObjectPack</code> | <code>format:git_pack_v2</code>, <code>object_format:sha1&#124;sha256</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>, <code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>object_count:uint53</code>, <code>inventory_blob_id:digest</code>, <code>inventory_blob_descriptor_id:digest</code> |\n4790|| <code>GitIndex</code> | <code>format:git_index</code>, <code>version:2&#124;3&#124;4</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>, <code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>entries:GitIndexEntry[0..65536]</code>, <code>entry_count:uint53</code>; entries sorted by path then stage, count equal to length |\n4791|| <code>GitIndexEntry</code> | <code>path:path</code>, <code>stage:uint8[0..3]</code>, <code>mode:uint32</code>, <code>oid:git-oid</code>, <code>intent_to_add:boolean</code>, <code>skip_worktree:boolean</code>, <code>assume_unchanged:boolean</code>, <code>fsmonitor_valid:boolean</code> |\n4792|| <code>GitSubmodule</code> | <code>path:path</code>, <code>repository_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>sanitized_url:sanitized-git-URL</code>, <code>gitlink_oid:git-oid</code>, <code>initialized:boolean</code>, <code>head:GitHead&#124;null</code>, <code>upstream_ref:git-ref&#124;null</code>, <code>object_pack:GitObjectPack&#124;null</code>, <code>index:GitIndex&#124;null</code>, <code>working_tree_manifest_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>submodules:GitSubmodule[0..256]&#124;null</code>, <code>features:GitFeatures&#124;null</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path&#124;null</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]&#124;null</code> |\n4793|| <code>GitFeatures</code> | <code>object_format:sha1&#124;sha256</code>, <code>filemode:boolean</code>, <code>symlinks:boolean</code>, <code>case_sensitive:boolean</code>, <code>precompose_unicode:boolean</code>, <code>sparse_checkout:boolean</code>, <code>sparse_patterns_blob_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>sparse_patterns_blob_descriptor_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>required_filter_names:sorted unique string[0..64]</code>, <code>lfs_required:boolean</code> |\n4794|\n4795|A <code>git-oid</code> is <code>sha1:</code> plus 40 lowercase hexadecimal\n4796|characters or <code>sha256:</code> plus 64, matching\n4797|<code>features.object_format</code>. A <code>git-ref</code> is a 1–1024 byte\n4798|fully qualified ref accepted by <code>git check-ref-format</code>; the literals\n4799|<code>HEAD</code> and abbreviated refs are forbidden. Remotes use the same\n4800|sanitization as Section 5.6.\n4801|\n4802|Each <code>GitObjectPack</code> contains only objects from the repository whose\n4803|descriptor owns it. A superproject pack contains every superproject object\n4804|needed to resolve its HEAD, recorded refs, and non-gitlink index entries\n4805|without network access. A mode-160000 gitlink OID is an opaque commit name in\n4806|the child repository and MUST NOT be required to resolve in the superproject\n4807|pack. Each initialized <code>GitSubmodule.object_pack</code> independently\n4808|contains the child objects needed to resolve that submodule's checked-out HEAD,\n4809|index, and nested state. Its inventory blob is UTF-8\n4810|lines <code>OID SP commit|tree|blob|tag SP DECIMAL_SIZE LF</code>, bytewise\n4811|sorted by OID, with no duplicate and exactly <code>object_count</code> lines.\n4812|The raw Git index blob and the logical entries MUST describe the same supported\n4813|index; unknown required extensions fail closed. Working-tree manifest bytes are\n4814|the actual post-index bytes, so staged and unstaged content remain distinct.\n4815|\n4816|<code>GitSubmodule.gitlink_oid</code> is exactly the OID of the stage-0,\n4817|mode-160000 entry for <code>GitSubmodule.path</code> in the containing\n4818|superproject's <code>GitIndex.entries</code>. Protocol 1.0.0 rejects a submodule\n4819|path with only conflict stages 1–3. The superproject HEAD-tree gitlink is a\n4820|derived value obtained by resolving that path in the tree named by the\n4821|containing member's <code>head.oid</code>; it is called\n4822|<code>head_tree_gitlink_oid</code> in fixture prose but is not an additional\n4823|wire member. The checked-out child commit is\n4824|<code>GitSubmodule.head.oid</code>. These three values are deliberately\n4825|independent so staged and unstaged pointer changes are preserved.\n4826|\n4827|An initialized submodule requires every state field after\n4828|<code>initialized</code> except <code>upstream_ref</code> to be non-null. Its\n4829|head is branch or detached, never unborn. Its head OID MUST resolve as a commit\n4830|in its own <code>GitSubmodule.object_pack</code>; it need not equal either\n4831|superproject pointer. An uninitialized submodule requires every state field after\n4832|<code>initialized</code> to be null. Nested submodules use the same exact shape;\n4833|the tree is acyclic, has depth at most 16, and contains at most 256 submodules\n4834|in total. This recursive state preserves staged, unstaged, untracked, cwd, and\n4835|project-configuration facts inside initialized submodules instead of assuming\n4836|they are clean.\n4837|\n4838|Sparse pattern blob and descriptor are either both non-null when sparse\n4839|checkout is true or both null when false. Every referenced working-tree,\n4840|managed-tree, and submodule manifest MUST occur in the workspace root's\n4841|transitive child closure. Every cwd directory and project-configuration path\n4842|MUST exist in that closure.\n4843|\n4844|The following language-neutral payload corpus is part of\n4845|<code>WS-GIT-ROUNDTRIP-1</code>. <code>base64url</code> is the exact unpadded\n4846|encoding of the blob bytes. Every payload is one chunk, so its complete Blob\n4847|Descriptor is reconstructed with schema <code>urn:ax:schema:blob</code>, version\n4848|<code>1.0.0</code>, the displayed blob ID, size and media type, and one\n4849|<code>{index:0,offset:0,size,chunk_id:blob_id}</code> entry. The displayed\n4850|descriptor ID is the JCS self-identity of that reconstructed descriptor.\n4851|\n4852|~~~json\n4853|{\n4854|  \"fixture\": \"ax-git-workspace-v1\",\n4855|  \"parent_commit\": \"sha1:602548b4fd46332c934667db9992b8bb00318c88\",\n4856|  \"child_commit\": \"sha1:25eec72bdd91287a7d68f206907a859b5a7b5524\",\n4857|  \"parent_object_count\": 7,\n4858|  \"child_object_count\": 3,\n4859|  \"parent_index_entries\": [\n4860|    \"100644 5461fe036f6cf55f98d75ee651c2b4cc13a80c66 0\\t.gitmodules\",\n4861|    \"100644 b6b0be997c9c8246cdd346dd7ece72140d74dee0 0\\tAGENTS.md\",\n4862|    \"100644 19d9cc8584ac2c7dcf57d2680375e80f099dc481 0\\tREADME.md\",\n4863|    \"160000 25eec72bdd91287a7d68f206907a859b5a7b5524 0\\tvendor/lib\"\n4864|  ],\n4865|  \"child_index_entries\": [\n4866|    \"100644 a69c0feac9815fe47cecb849931d858109a5a0c9 0\\tREADME.md\"\n4867|  ],\n4868|  \"payloads\": [\n4869|    {\"label\":\"agent_file\",\"size\":6,\"media_type\":\"text/plain\",\"base64url\":\"YWdlbnQK\",\"blob_id\":\"sha256:d20bc21bb3c7736d8d03ade3ddb4c68b665cdfbca6f6df0f7fdd192f37f59060\",\"descriptor_id\":\"sha256:ffa55edaa3cc8c1263644441fd01896bcaf92d91c55ae9bd91edcabb1f408ba9\"},\n4870|    {\"label\":\"base_file\",\"size\":5,\"media_type\":\"text/plain\",\"base64url\":\"YmFzZQo\",\"blob_id\":\"sha256:f34848ca92665c342abd5816c9e3eda0e82180671195362bcd0080544a3bc2ac\",\"descriptor_id\":\"sha256:3d47b1837f2c69c881fd924e94e7296b297d1de4353743ba45007dca5e05c8f9\"},\n4871|    {\"label\":\"staged_file\",\"size\":7,\"media_type\":\"text/plain\",\"base64url\":\"c3RhZ2VkCg\",\"blob_id\":\"sha256:9ac007af3de930baf647288da0c843b26a5f046a3fe1351f1bb039b242d22cdf\",\"descriptor_id\":\"sha256:2a383ef6cac04d7f52b750dc3256bca620883943c4d4cabf31aa644f630b539e\"},\n4872|    {\"label\":\"working_file\",\"size\":8,\"media_type\":\"text/plain\",\"base64url\":\"d29ya2luZwo\",\"blob_id\":\"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\",\"descriptor_id\":\"sha256:f3fe5a9c5e1ef041645b84b5618a4a2d6e4184dbd11c21b92b0bdcaa482ad7ab\"},\n4873|    {\"label\":\"notes_file\",\"size\":6,\"media_type\":\"text/plain\",\"base64url\":\"bm90ZXMK\",\"blob_id\":\"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\",\"descriptor_id\":\"sha256:de864d26dacd33a1970e78c2c5f588708bb17905fa0a1c712d6a40ddee182e73\"},\n4874|    {\"label\":\"child_file\",\"size\":6,\"media_type\":\"text/plain\",\"base64url\":\"Y2hpbGQK\",\"blob_id\":\"sha256:2fa14f53e6b15cac9ac77846c7be87862c2a7e9ec0c6cea319db939317f126ed\",\"descriptor_id\":\"sha256:089ed22190957336a4f4710831c1ac65e2176773f3df4cf52589103f7571c0a4\"},\n4875|    {\"label\":\"gitmodules_file\",\"size\":86,\"media_type\":\"text/plain\",\"base64url\":\"W3N1Ym1vZHVsZSAidmVuZG9yL2xpYiJdCglwYXRoID0gdmVuZG9yL2xpYgoJdXJsID0gc3NoOi8vZ2l0QGdpdGh1Yi5jb20vcmVsdXgvbGliLmdpdAo\",\"blob_id\":\"sha25