{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d47f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07dba-037c-7562-bb6d-27534398ea11"},"sequence":2202,"recorded_at":1780531400004399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"cf9a10d3-9e0b-4b82-9c42-412fe95e7b1b"},"task_id":"cf9a10d3-9e0b-4b82-9c42-412fe95e7b1b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"cf9a10d3-9e0b-4b82-9c42-412fe95e7b1b","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 2226-2232\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-```bash\n-go generate ./internal/catalog\n-go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.5.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n-go test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\n-```\n-\n-## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\n+```bash\n+go generate ./internal/catalog\n+go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.5.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n+go test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\n+```\n+\n+## Git Repository and Index Snapshot\n+\n+[`internal/gitsnap`](internal/gitsnap) captures the live Git state Sections\n+10.4 (`kind = git` member) and 12.1-12.3 require: repository identity,\n+sanitized remotes, HEAD/ref mode, worktree metadata, index stages and\n+flags, staged and unstaged deltas, and tracked file modes. The production\n+entry is `Capture`, which drives the Git executable through a `Runner`\n+seam (`ExecGitRunner` in production, a scripted fake in tests) with\n+`GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, so a capture never takes an index or reference\n+lock. `Capture` mutates no durable state: it returns a complete validated\n+snapshot or a `*Refusal` naming the registry gate that fired, never a\n+partial snapshot.\n+\n+Sixteen refusal gates cover the scope, each named in `gates.go` with its\n+specification clause and driven through `Capture` by its proving test\n+(see `gateProvingTests` in `census_test.go`). The gate census counts\n+literal `refuse(Gate...)` call sites in non-test production files after\n+stripping comments and string literals: 16 of 16 registry rows have at\n+least one site, and 3 of 3 refusal codes are live. The census ships\n+controls: comment and string-literal plants stay uncounted, an\n+unregistered planted gate reddens, and an alias-bound call stays\n+invisible, which is the stated blind spot the package upholds by always\n+invoking `refuse` directly.\n+\n+Arithmetic edges are proven at the production entry in both directions:\n+remotes accept 16 and refuse 17, index entries accept 65536 and refuse\n+65537 with `capability_unavailable`, identity accepts 256 characters and\n+refuses 257, stage accepts 3 and refuses 4 (the `TM-GIT-N2` mutation),\n+and index version accepts 2-4 while refusing 1 and 5. The identity bound\n+counts characters, not bytes: a 256-character multibyte identity\n+captures. Repeat captures of a quiesced repository encode\n+byte-identically; a HEAD, index, or delta stream that moves mid-capture\n+is refused with `workspace_conflict` after a closing re-read, and a\n+retry heals. The `WS-GIT-ROUNDTRIP-1` parent and child index lines are\n+quoted verbatim from the specification and parsed through `Capture` into\n+the normative wire entries.\n+\n+Stated bounds: object packs, raw index blobs, untracked and ignored\n+bytes, symlink targets, submodule recursion, and working-tree manifests\n+belong to sibling leaves of the same story and are not produced here;\n+the `entry_count` wire-mismatch refusal belongs to\n+`internal/canonicaljson`; refusal codes are diagnostic strings in the\n+specification vocabulary and are not `axerror` envelopes. Run the\n+package gates with:\n+\n+```bash\n+go test ./internal/gitsnap -count=1\n+go test ./internal/gitsnap -cover -count=1\n+```\n+\n+## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\n"}}}
