{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d7f1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07dba-037c-7562-bb6d-27534398ea11"},"sequence":2643,"recorded_at":1780531400005281,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0442ca47-9067-45d4-a281-7f472a3b7616"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f05054ad-136a-4222-aa34-f3d108faafe1"},"task_id":"f05054ad-136a-4222-aa34-f3d108faafe1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f05054ad-136a-4222-aa34-f3d108faafe1","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-81-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 30 LOGBOOK.md 2>&1; date +%Y-%m-%d\\\\ %H%M\",\n  \"description\": \"Read logbook head and current date\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-07\\n\\n### 9ny4xl: R1–R6 closed — probe-availability claims corrected, marker census measures effect, catalog directive pinned\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260907-9ny4xl (story final leaf). `internal/cigate` claim tests + effect census + splitter tests + `doc.go`, `internal/catalog` directive pin, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` comments + freshness guard, README CI table + 20 probe notes, 2249 correction below. Leaves 1–5 production untouched; `claims.go` production changed only in comments; `catalog.go` production unchanged.\\n- R1: the capability-claims comment and the 2249 entry stated `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site; `claims.go:235` reads it into the availability map. Both now state what `doc.go` states: the gate reads `Available` from its input states (both postures driven), and what reaches no availability reader is the live probe outcome (`ProbeStates` feeds only `CapabilityIDs`, which drops availability). New `TestAvailabilityFieldDrivesVerdict` refuses/admits the same claim across postures (battery N-avail-false/true killed).\\n- R2: the derive-targets comment named the grep + size check as the fail-closed guards. Re-measured with a real empty-leg replica (`secconftest` + fuzzless `axerror`): grep refuses nothing (pipeline status discarded), `test -s` passes (8 lines), only the count pin refuses (8 vs 13, exit 1). Comment now names the pin; neighbouring steps audited (PASS-guard loops, gofmt/coverage/fixture count guards, target-match diff, elapsed grep) — no same mistake.\\n- R3: the marker census measured occurrence while markers classified 0 of 2 mentions. New `TestEveryNonClaimMarkerClassifiesCorpusSentence` asserts the resolving arm per mention from the production predicates cross-checked against the production verdict, and requires every marker to sole-classify at least one corpus sentence. 20 probe notes added to the README CI section (one sole-classifier per marker); measured distribution negation 2 / marker 20 / refused 0. README cell corrected to \\\"negated or marker-classified non-claim context\\\". Old corpus + new census fails (battery C-old-corpus); dropped-list X3 now dies (was a survivor).\\n- R4: new `TestSameBlockSentencesSplitOnTerminal` (period/bang/query rows, same-block negated+positive pair) kills the paragraph-granularity narrowing (N-split-X1) and the dot-only narrowing (N-split-dot-only).\\n- R5 (bound, re-measured this session): 13/13 smoke targets print `fuzz: elapsed`; `secconftest/FuzzRedactCorpus` + all four `canonicaljson` targets spend `-fuzztime=100x` on baseline coverage and never print `now fuzzing` (8 reach mutation). Stated in the README row and the smoke-step comment with the escape (budget/corpus change moves it silently).\\n- R6 (bound ANSWERED): the rev2 \\\"Linux execution unverified\\\" unknown is closed by the landing PR run — PR #36 (STORY-260830-1i3qu7, merged 2026-09-06) shows `Conformance fixtures (ubuntu-latest, internal/secprim)` and `(ubuntu-latest, internal/secconftest)` pass in both runs, with macOS legs and every other job green (`gh pr checks 36`, observed this session).\\n- CARRIED (pre-existing, fixed here): `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` disarmed the generator while the token survived and the freshness diff stayed clean (reproduced: old step exits 0 on the rewrite). Fix: anchored `grep -c '^//go:generate'` pin in the freshness step + committed `TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm`; the rewrite now fails the guard (exit 1) and the pin while catalog/cataloggen stay otherwise green (battery G-directive-space, behavioral suite executed).\\n- RECORDED (pre-existing, not fixed — traceability scope): `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` is a `bytes.Contains` gate over `ci.yml`: moving the Vet step's `run: go vet ./...` into a YAML comment keeps it green (doubly blind — `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` carries the same substring). Re-attacked this session (PASS on the blinded tree, ci.yml restored byte-identical). At HEAD before every leaf of both stories; named here beside the `go:generate` one per the rev2 verdict.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_outcome.md` (5/5 AC rows with call sites, battery table, tree OID, exact changed paths) + `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_mutants.log` + `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_change-request.patch` on the board task. Battery 14 applied / 14 killed / 0 survivors (narrowing 10 incl. the token-preserving directive rewrite, arm-deletion 3, census-only 1; C-old-corpus census control; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct harness rows; audit-only 0 — no AST audit in this CR's scope).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (23 ok), `-race ./...` exit 0 (23 ok, full repo), `-cover` exit 0 (cigate 90.5%, secprim 94.4%, secconftest 92.6%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (60 contracts / 98 cases, unchanged), catalog current, capability-claims + contract-preservation steps verbatim 6/6 + 6/6, fuzz smoke 13/13 elapsed (5 baseline-only, 8 mutation).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps). Story-final CR: no board element created under STORY-260905-3t31e9; follow-up needs are listed in the outcome, not the board.\\n\\n### 33xcnc round 2: review F1/F2/F3 closed test-only, 70/71 battery on the corrected 101-exit denominator\\n- SCOPE (test-only; no production touched, frozen files intact): `internal/environ/shape_census_test.go` (load-bearing delegation pins + 9 synthetic decoy controls), `tuple_agreement_test.go` (uppercase-hex fingerprint vector), `frame_agreement_test.go` (per-member duplicate sweeper over 30 production-derived keys × 4 judges), `decode_unit_test.go` (R_digestnonstr downstream pin), `internal/provhost/protocol_test.go` (DecodeResponse per-member duplicate test, 6 derived + 4 foreign keys).\\n- F1 (decoy defeated the gate): `pinsCheckDelegation`/`pinsDelegation` required only an `environ` reference, so `_, _ = environ.CheckDigest(raw)` + a regrown `ParseDigest(ToLower)` copy stayed green while `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` admitted uppercase-hex fingerprints `environ` refuses. Fix: helpers must be exactly `return environ.Twin(args)` with twin-name match; wrappers must attribute the owner verdict to reused non-blank names with no other call, plus a duplicate-rule check. The plant now fails `TestCheckHelpersDelegateToEnviron` AND `TestTupleAgreementAcrossFacades/uppercase_fingerprint_refused`; harness mutants D1/D2 report `suites=behavioral,census`.\\n- F2 (duplicate class measured at one key): narrowing `duplicate && key != K` survived 6/8 response keys and 7/10 owner keys. Fix: derivation-backed sweepers (member sets derived from tuple/observation/response/scan-request production; new members auto-swept) through `DecodeTuple`/`CheckScanRequest`/`DecodeManifest`/`DecodeResponse`/`DecodeStrictObject`. Battery adds 8 owner + 6 retained narrowing mutants, one per survived key. Survivor honest-report: first `P_dupnarrow_provider_id` run SURVIVED and exposed a real test gap (foreign `provider_id` missing from the envelope sweeper); key added, mutant re-run KILLED.\\n- F3 (denominator basis): corrected — 31 refuse sites + 59 bool-false + 11 `&Fault{}` frame exits = 101 (105 counting the 4 bool-`return <expr>` arms: CheckEnvironmentID/CheckSemver/isNull/rawUint53-forward). The \\\"27 of 100\\\" figure was the corrected basis pre-ladder-guard; 90 was the uncorrected one. Harness derives all three components at runtime; F3 residue exits attacked by N1/M15/M15n/M16/M17/M17n inside the previously excluded 11.\\n- EVIDENCE: battery `/tmp/mutbattery_leaf6/run.py` + `battery.log` + `results.json`: 70 killed / 71 applied (49 narrowing incl. D1 token-preserving delegation decoy + 8 owner + 6 retained duplicate narrowings; 17 arm-deletion incl. D2; 3 census-only; 1 audit-only; H1 NOT_APPLIED + H2 COMPILE_FAIL distinct rows; 1 predicted survivor R_digestnonstr, now property-pinned by `TestDigestBridgeRefusesEmptyDownstream`). Mutant table + outcome attached as round-2 resources.\\n- GATES: `go build` + `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` build/vet exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok), `go test ./... -race` exit 0 (23 ok, full repo — no race bound this round), `-cover` (env 92.4/sess 82.0/dir 87.7/ph 86.0/scalar 90.1/invcore 70.2).\\n- STATUS: handed off to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n2026-09-08 0137\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8457,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2115,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
